(7404511, 978498, 38032, '<td valign="top">I don''t remember how I got here. To this image I mean.<br/> <br/>But I hadn''t seen the original image, just your profile photo. I laughed when I saw it but then I realized it got some pretty special comments. It reminds me of aesthetics and criticism class - questioning what art is ... but it seems like social media has turned <strike>everyone</strike> many into critics - not only of the work itself, but full-on analyzing and evaluating the person who chose to submit it. There is an assumed context - normally a negative one, associated with things people don''t want to talk about.<br/> <br/>Anyhow, kind of fun to come across this nice low-scoring, highly polarizing image ;]</td>', 'I don''t remember how I got here. To this image I mean. But I hadn''t seen the original image, just your profile photo. I laughed when I saw it but then I realized it got some pretty special comments. It reminds me of aesthetics and criticism class - questioning what art is ... but it seems like social media has turned everyone many into critics - not only of the work itself, but full-on analyzing and evaluating the person who chose to submit it. There is an assumed context - normally a negative one, associated with things people don''t want to talk about. Anyhow, kind of fun to come across this nice low-scoring, highly polarizing image ;]', '2015-09-14 16:09:53.000000', NULL, 0);
COMMIT;
